00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.790
Hire somebody that is good at it.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.720
Know it well enough to know
if they're doing it well.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.030
This portion is like, with me,

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.950
so I think this is when
you need to get selfish.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.246
Like need to ask your question.

00:00:20.246 --> 00:00:22.829
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.810
Hiring is guessing, firing is knowing.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.680
Like you gotta go fast.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.810
That's how you get shit down,

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.160
that's how you figure stuff out.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.960
This is the television

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.243
and television is the radio.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.263
So Four Ds motherfuckers.

00:00:39.263 --> 00:00:41.470
- With the three studios,
I can't be everywhere

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:42.303
all at once,

00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:43.585
- That's right.

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:44.900
- And it's really easy for me

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.560
to get the wind taken out of my sails.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.320
- When one of the
locations isn't delivering

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.310
on your standard?

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.440
- It's the individual people themselves.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.433
- Right.

00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:56.266
- So I am like crazy about this,

00:00:56.266 --> 00:00:57.420
I'm super, super driven.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.370
I know everybody can be
amazing and successful,

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:01.980
and they just want to pay their bills.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.610
So I'm dealing with apathy.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:04.960
- Your employees?

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.190
- Yeah.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:08.100
- Okay, so a couple things.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.470
This is really funny 'cause
this is probably the first thing

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.210
I ever started really talking
to my dad about as a kid,

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:18.003
as somebody who had like gifted wisdom.

00:01:20.771 --> 00:01:22.471
What keeps me super mellow is like

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.740
my thought process and
the things I do well

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:30.550
are gifted DNA and circumstances.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.680
So I never get high on my own supply.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.880
It's just so weird that this
is probably the first thing

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.920
I started talking to my dad
about when I was 15 years old.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.550
I looked at my dad one
time when we were driving

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:42.510
and I said, Dad if they were you,

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.030
they wouldn't work for you.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:47.010
This is something we talk
about 28 years later.

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:49.200
My dad brings up that statement.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.290
He's like, you were a kid.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:55.460
Your ideology for what
everybody should be doing

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.723
is the quickest way for you to struggle.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.010
There's a very big,

00:02:01.008 --> 00:02:04.890
like I have enormous
energy on impacting people

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.724
in a good way whether
it's directly attributed

00:02:07.724 --> 00:02:09.939
to the people that work
with me or the masses.

00:02:09.939 --> 00:02:10.772
Whether that's through heart or hustle,

00:02:10.772 --> 00:02:12.150
whatever it may be.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.640
But you have to become deeply aware that

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.700
there's only so many
things you can handle.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.210
The other thing that it really leads to is

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:26.073
it leads into you trying to
control something you can't.

00:02:27.307 --> 00:02:29.650
This compounds.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.168
And takes over.

00:02:31.168 --> 00:02:32.270
- Yeah, for 10 years.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.450
- It's a losing proposition.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:38.037
First of all, there's a lot of bad in it.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.760
There's a lot of ego and
a lot of your own shit

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.650
that you need to really
understand that truth.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.200
It's the same bad that I have.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.710
I create entitlement because I try to

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.513
take on too much on myself.

00:02:54.587 --> 00:02:56.550
So you gotta be careful with this one.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.390
Here's what I would say.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:01.630
Your job as somebody that
sits at the top of something

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.630
is to put players in the
best position to succeed.

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.660
Once you've done that,
you've gotta allow them

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.560
to do their thing.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.740
You're a capitalist trying to deploy

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:16.680
almost socialist, communist ideology.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.280
You can't control everything.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.880
Like, there's nothing
wrong with paying your,

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.520
what's wrong with paying your bills?

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.030
- They're capable of so much more.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.520
- Says who?

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.520
You don't know them.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.340
You don't know them.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:32.080
I know Caleb solidly.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.755
I know Nick solidly.

00:03:33.755 --> 00:03:34.947
Like, you know don't know.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.963
You're fuckin' spouse and
parents don't know you.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.313
Right?

00:03:40.313 --> 00:03:41.530
Let's get to real talk.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.700
There's not a single person on earth

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.900
that actually knows you.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.470
Every single person has
certain little subtle things

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:49.260
that they still have not
articulated to the world.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.343
To not one person.

00:03:52.781 --> 00:03:54.253
You're being ideological.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.623
To scratch your own itch.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.830
You have to understand that.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:04.750
I think a bigger thing is
where are you going with that?

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.980
I think if you're going
into a place of like,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.530
they could be so much and
we could win together,

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.270
which would make sense to me, right?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.880
Let me help you be a better employee,

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.750
you'll do better, we'll do better, right?

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:16.363
You're better off firing them.

00:04:19.439 --> 00:04:21.251
- I knew you were gonna say that.

00:04:21.251 --> 00:04:22.110
I hate firing people.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:22.993
- Me too!

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:25.253
Me too.

00:04:25.253 --> 00:04:28.600
But me hating firing people creates,

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.700
what I do with it is I create
entitlement and protect people

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.740
at my cost which makes
them think they're better

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:34.920
than they are.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.640
Your not firing people is your imposing

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.183
an ideology on them.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.670
You're making it about,

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:44.690
you could be so much,

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:47.050
you're putting it on
them, instead of yourself.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:47.990
You don't want to fire them

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.790
because they're not
capable of over-delivering

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:51.820
or delivering on the
standard of what you need

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.100
for your business.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.400
And so they way you're
deploying that resentment

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.960
is deploying them to feel bad
that they're not achieving

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.840
they're capability predicated on something

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.390
that you need them to do in the context

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:04.383
of your four walls.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.183
- So I just need to get
the right people in there.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.490
- I'm at my best when I fire fast,

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:13.640
when I know it's wrong.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.410
And I do that rarely
'cause I don't like it.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.043
But I've gotten better at it.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.650
But you shouldn't create, you know,

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.540
resentment comes out
in very different ways.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:32.350
When I'm resenting something,
I'm razzing people.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.830
Like I'll make jokes.

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.763
That's my way of getting it out.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:39.820
You're not doing any
favors looking somebody

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.320
dead in the eye and say
you could be so much more.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.110
It's doing nobody a favor.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.130
It's not doing you a favor,
it's not doing them a favor.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.120
What you need to be thinking about is

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:48.340
first and foremost, the number one thing

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.800
you need to be thinking about is

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:53.830
the three managers, or
the one regional manager,

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.040
the people that are actually
responsible in the trenches,

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.983
that's who needs to be a hundred.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.540
You fix that, you fix everything.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.423
Don't focus on the
sink, focus on the well.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:09.310
Everything I'm worried about
in the thousand employees here

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:12.150
is predicated on my 11 direct reports

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.533
that run those departments.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:18.673
Got it?

00:06:18.673 --> 00:06:19.506
- It's on the managers.

00:06:19.506 --> 00:06:20.660
- The managers.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:21.920
If the three managers are perfect,

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.572
then you'll be set.

00:06:23.572 --> 00:06:24.405
- And they're not.

00:06:24.405 --> 00:06:25.413
- No shit.

00:06:25.413 --> 00:06:26.246
(laughing)

00:06:26.246 --> 00:06:27.079
I know.

00:06:27.079 --> 00:06:29.090
I know, that's how it works.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:30.560
That's how businesses work.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.660
You've only got two variables
that you're talking about.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.410
This is why it's easy
for me to understand.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.850
I know that they're not right.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.600
And then underneath that,
the employees you have

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:41.380
either they're under performing
'cause the manger blows

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.470
and you know it.

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:43.780
Or they've just been around for a while

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:45.680
and you have actual human emotion to them.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:47.070
And those are both valid.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:49.820
But the quickest thing that
will make you so much happier

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.320
is to make sure the three
managers are phenomenal.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.420
You have three, I would
assume, per location?

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:59.550
- They basically deal
with all the happy stuff.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.610
And if anything goes wrong

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:03.600
I'm the one that has to
come in to deal with that.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:04.560
- You've created that.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.170
Just like I created it here.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:07.840
You need to un-create that.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.020
And what is fine at a
smaller business level

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:11.740
and why it worked for me at Wine Library,

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.610
when it's smaller there's a level of fine,

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.101
but if you have ambition
and for it to grow,

00:07:16.101 --> 00:07:18.620
you need to get the value out of the way

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:19.453
you're compensating.

00:07:19.453 --> 00:07:21.970
You're better off compensating more

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:25.233
and letting people do the
defense and the shit as well.

00:07:27.301 --> 00:07:28.134
- Okay.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:29.943
Got it.

00:07:29.943 --> 00:07:30.776
- Got it?

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:33.430
- [Man] Two questions.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.360
The first one, with combat vet being

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:38.500
kind of my main business,

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.363
about 45 percent of my business,

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:45.780
but I was not in the military,
I was not in law enforcement,

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:50.290
so it's a target market
that I appreciate very much,

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:52.410
but I'm not really a part of.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:55.580
- I think that as long
as you're authentic,

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.840
you know, there is a small subset.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:01.500
In any subculture there's
always a part of that group

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.170
that will always be like,
well you're not one of us

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.960
so you have no permission here.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:06.910
But if you speak to admiring something,

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.220
as long as you're clear cut about that

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:12.550
and not hiding and trying to avoid,

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:13.800
I think,

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.620
I think you'd be surprised on how much of

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.540
a non-issue that is for the 89 percent.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:20.523
- Okay 'cause one of my manger--

00:08:20.523 --> 00:08:22.270
- 'cause the 11 percent, yeah,

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.933
- Was military, retired military,

00:08:25.832 --> 00:08:27.300
and they have their stuff made in China.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.610
But they don't tell anybody that.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:32.550
They're like, oh we're
military owned and operated.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:33.440
So they get a lot of business.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:36.202
I feel like they get a lot
of business because of that.

00:08:36.202 --> 00:08:38.920
- And the consumer's always right.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:40.250
Like you can't focus on that.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:41.210
You get two moves.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:42.570
You're more than welcome to
make a video and be like,

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:46.540
look, I have deep admiration
for our law enforcement

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.920
and our military and here's why.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:52.340
And I'm extremely proud that
we make our product in America

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.630
and we have competitors in the marketplace

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.090
who've been in this space,

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.710
but they make their product in China.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:59.460
And you the customer should decide.

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:02.240
- Would you say that even though--

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.073
- Yes.

00:09:03.073 --> 00:09:05.140
- Even though they claim to make--

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:09.480
- I would, because that's how I roll.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:10.683
You don't need to.

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:15.433
I'm not a big fan of
dwelling without action.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.830
Either you never dwell about it again,

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:20.863
or you mention it.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.083
But the middle blows.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:26.950
That's what you're doing.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:28.953
That's the game.

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.350
The reason I don't complain,

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:33.780
the reason I genuinely don't is

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:35.050
I've got a very basic thesis.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.380
Either I do something about it,

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.420
or if I've decided I don't
want to do something about it,

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.730
which is many things,

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:42.900
I don't do, there's certain
things that cross places

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:44.340
where I'm not comfortable,

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:45.570
and I keep my mouth shut.

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.510
'Cause there's too much
energy wasted in dwelling.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:51.003
You're competitor has you on defense.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.823
I know nothing about my competitors.

00:09:59.451 --> 00:10:00.284
- [Man] It's not really relevant.

00:10:00.284 --> 00:10:02.353
- The consumer's the
only thing that matters.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:04.653
I just don't care.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.660
The whole like, you can learn from them.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:09.710
I'll learn it anyway.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.410
Plus I'm not worried about the past.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.510
This is what's great about
being in the trenches.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:16.343
Right?

00:10:17.675 --> 00:10:21.240
I have come to learn that
growing up in a liquor store

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:22.580
and a baseball card table,

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.760
my whole life was I'm behind something,

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:28.550
somebody's coming, I watch what
they do, something happens.

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:29.423
Consumer.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.940
The end.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.570
So yes, I would, because
I would like to create

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.760
the conversation of that.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.043
Because I think it's a
competitive advantage.

00:10:38.886 --> 00:10:40.300
Especially if they're
not authentic about it

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.360
because then you can get,

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.000
you know, people are very curious.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:46.410
You put it out there, people
start digging, they find.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.243
Right?

00:10:47.243 --> 00:10:48.320
On a podcast the other day I mentioned

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:49.940
that I was in a Wrestle Mania.

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:51.360
I showed up at this
Wrestle Mania and I said

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.990
I was once in another Wrestle Mania.

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:54.600
I got the clip now, somebody found it.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:57.010
People dig, people dig.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:11:00.120
You set it up, let somebody
else make the expose

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:01.460
if you don't want to go all the way there.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.073
Innuendoing is fun.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.844
- [Man] And I can keep putting clips of us

00:11:05.844 --> 00:11:09.843
manufacturing the chips
and nobody else can.

00:11:09.843 --> 00:11:10.676
- That's what I would do.

00:11:10.676 --> 00:11:12.130
I'd put out the clip
and be like here we are!

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.560
In Iowa making the chip.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.000
