00:32:57.380 --> 00:32:59.250
I'm managing our MailChimp myself

00:32:59.250 --> 00:33:00.540
and really kind of bringing all this in.

00:33:00.540 --> 00:33:02.840
- I'm a big fan of pulling
in and pulling back out.

00:33:02.840 --> 00:33:03.970
- [Man] And that was
going to be my question

00:33:03.970 --> 00:33:06.655
is that people say well
that's not sustainable,

00:33:06.655 --> 00:33:07.554
that's not sustainable.

00:33:07.554 --> 00:33:08.528
And I'm like, yeah I know.

00:33:08.528 --> 00:33:09.361
- In theory.

00:33:09.361 --> 00:33:10.430
- [Man] The next three to five years.

00:33:10.430 --> 00:33:11.840
- Right, in theory.

00:33:11.840 --> 00:33:13.680
- [Man] How do you choose what to give up?

00:33:13.680 --> 00:33:15.546
When do you starting
thinking about the future?

00:33:15.546 --> 00:33:19.938
- The delta between the
things I like the most.

00:33:19.938 --> 00:33:20.771
- [Man] 'Cause I want to hold it all

00:33:20.771 --> 00:33:21.867
for as long as possible, right?

00:33:21.867 --> 00:33:24.720
- The things I like
the most and the things

00:33:24.720 --> 00:33:26.630
I'm best at, I keep.

00:33:26.630 --> 00:33:27.920
And the things I don't like

00:33:27.920 --> 00:33:29.150
and the things I'm not best at

00:33:29.150 --> 00:33:31.522
I try to systematically
give away over time.

00:33:31.522 --> 00:33:33.330
- [Man] Okay.

00:33:33.330 --> 00:33:34.460
Cool just look at what--

00:33:34.460 --> 00:33:36.340
- Self awareness and happiness

00:33:36.340 --> 00:33:37.890
is the answer to your question.

00:33:38.970 --> 00:33:39.803
There's just certain,

00:33:39.803 --> 00:33:41.390
like what are we doing here?

00:33:41.390 --> 00:33:44.020
You have a business to
do you what you like.

00:33:44.020 --> 00:33:45.450
Like fuck it, if you can't,

00:33:45.450 --> 00:33:47.270
you know how many people build a business

00:33:47.270 --> 00:33:48.527
that then the business eats them

00:33:48.527 --> 00:33:49.823
and it becomes a job?

00:33:50.710 --> 00:33:53.300
And the thing you didn't want
to do like everybody else

00:33:53.300 --> 00:33:55.224
or the thing you ran away
from becomes the thing

00:33:55.224 --> 00:33:58.703
with the added pressure and
loneliness of entrepreneurship?

00:34:01.370 --> 00:34:05.293
So the things I like and
the things I'm best at.

00:34:06.220 --> 00:34:07.053
You know?

00:34:08.440 --> 00:34:09.340
But there is,

00:34:09.340 --> 00:34:12.470
I love treading everything back in.

00:34:12.470 --> 00:34:13.820
- [Man] It's exciting
and fun and I love it.

00:34:13.820 --> 00:34:15.190
- You also hone your skills

00:34:15.190 --> 00:34:17.350
and then you get better at
judging the people you bring in

00:34:17.350 --> 00:34:18.183
the next time.

00:34:18.183 --> 00:34:19.800
All of a sudden, your email marketing head

00:34:19.800 --> 00:34:22.210
is not going to be able to
trick you that they suck

00:34:22.210 --> 00:34:23.553
because you know MailChimp.

00:34:25.620 --> 00:34:26.683
I love that feeling.

00:34:28.860 --> 00:34:29.693
I love it.

00:34:31.810 --> 00:34:32.720
You know?

00:34:32.720 --> 00:34:34.010
- [Man] Follow up question.

00:34:34.010 --> 00:34:35.327
What's the most effective way

00:34:35.327 --> 00:34:37.330
