00:34:37.330 --> 00:34:38.770
I find it so weird--

00:34:38.770 --> 00:34:39.720
- Firing.

00:34:39.720 --> 00:34:40.553
- [Man] Firing?

00:34:40.553 --> 00:34:41.386
- Firing.

00:34:41.386 --> 00:34:42.270
- [Man] Firing, okay.

00:34:42.270 --> 00:34:44.420
- Money where your mouth is.

00:34:44.420 --> 00:34:46.450
Culture's easy if you're
willing to fire people

00:34:46.450 --> 00:34:48.623
that produce money that are assholes.

00:34:49.940 --> 00:34:52.069
- [Man] Firing, I actually
don't mind firing.

00:34:52.069 --> 00:34:52.959
- Good, firing.

00:34:52.959 --> 00:34:54.462
- [Man] I don't mind firing.

00:34:54.462 --> 00:34:57.295
- So to me, what's that?

00:34:57.295 --> 00:34:58.130
- [Man] It's just as important as hiring.

00:34:58.130 --> 00:34:59.430
Hiring and firing, you need to do that.

00:34:59.430 --> 00:35:01.480
- Firing's way more important.

00:35:01.480 --> 00:35:02.313
Way more.

00:35:02.313 --> 00:35:04.320
Because hiring is guessing.

00:35:04.320 --> 00:35:05.423
Firing is knowing.

00:35:08.420 --> 00:35:09.678
Caleb's ...

00:35:09.678 --> 00:35:11.928
(laughing)

00:35:13.962 --> 00:35:15.468
- [Man] You know that feeling.

00:35:15.468 --> 00:35:16.551
That's funny.

00:35:18.840 --> 00:35:21.210
- The way I hire, when
I'm left to my vices,

00:35:21.210 --> 00:35:23.853
like cool, yeah, interested, c'mon!

00:35:25.225 --> 00:35:26.940
- [Man] Sign me up!

00:35:26.940 --> 00:35:28.840
So you're saying your firing
sets the tone for the culture.

00:35:28.840 --> 00:35:29.911
- I do believe that, yes.

00:35:29.911 --> 00:35:30.744
- [Man] 'Cause everyone
sees that as an example of

00:35:30.744 --> 00:35:31.577
cool, we're not doing that.

00:35:31.577 --> 00:35:32.850
- There's nothing better
than firing somebody

00:35:32.850 --> 00:35:35.430
who's cancerous in culture.

00:35:35.430 --> 00:35:37.493
It builds confidence.

00:35:38.860 --> 00:35:42.210
I'm very big on that, and
then just articulating it.

00:35:42.210 --> 00:35:43.810
I mean every day people come in here,

00:35:43.810 --> 00:35:44.800
like into my office,

00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:49.800
Gary, like you know, people
love fuckin' theoretics.

00:35:50.175 --> 00:35:52.166
Gary what are we doing here?

00:35:52.166 --> 00:35:54.320
(chuckling)

00:35:54.320 --> 00:35:55.930
I'm like, I put out content every,

00:35:55.930 --> 00:35:58.340
I mean, every day I've
articulated that we're building

00:35:58.340 --> 00:36:01.205
a machine that sells shit so I can buy a,

00:36:01.205 --> 00:36:03.480
like it's the most,

00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:04.313
it's crazy.

00:36:04.313 --> 00:36:05.440
People that have been here six years,

00:36:05.440 --> 00:36:06.550
