00:38:07.580 --> 00:38:09.803
So we're interviewing, so she's not here.

00:38:09.803 --> 00:38:13.044
When we did Sasha, assumed the COO roles

00:38:13.044 --> 00:38:16.540
so I'm the CEO, COO, CSO I guess

00:38:16.540 --> 00:38:18.500
for all intents and
purpose, though I'm not.

00:38:18.500 --> 00:38:19.930
Ebbs and flows.

00:38:19.930 --> 00:38:22.580
I'm gonna hire somebody and
you know, ebbs and flows.

00:38:25.735 --> 00:38:26.568
- [Man] Thank you.

00:38:26.568 --> 00:38:27.401
- By the way there's another one.

00:38:27.401 --> 00:38:28.234
Talk to people.

00:38:30.090 --> 00:38:32.910
Once you have a feel of
what every person wants

00:38:32.910 --> 00:38:34.870
and once you create a
place that's safe for them

00:38:34.870 --> 00:38:35.960
to tell you the truth,

00:38:35.960 --> 00:38:36.930
you got a prayer.

00:38:36.930 --> 00:38:38.630
And take it from somebody
who's really trying,

00:38:38.630 --> 00:38:40.000
it's super hard.

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:42.570
They'll tell you, I send
out fuckin' emails like

00:38:42.570 --> 00:38:45.470
once every three months with
a video of me like, come to,

00:38:45.470 --> 00:38:47.950
literally the video I
did last Friday was it?

00:38:47.950 --> 00:38:50.330
I was like, if you think
that if you came and told me

00:38:50.330 --> 00:38:52.860
your boss is a dick face,
that I would fire you

00:38:52.860 --> 00:38:54.760
or you're in trouble, you
don't know where you work.

00:38:54.760 --> 00:38:57.133
Yet that's the biggest fear of
every person that works here.

00:39:00.080 --> 00:39:00.913
- [Man] Humans.

00:39:00.913 --> 00:39:02.290
- Humans.

00:39:02.290 --> 00:39:05.130
But, the one thing I can
control is what I do.

00:39:05.130 --> 00:39:06.920
So even though I know

00:39:06.920 --> 00:39:08.320
that 80 percent won't act.

00:39:08.320 --> 00:39:10.160
It doesn't stop me from
putting out the content

00:39:10.160 --> 00:39:12.530
in company-wide emails
once every couple months

00:39:12.530 --> 00:39:13.780
whenever I feel inspired.

00:39:14.700 --> 00:39:15.703
I keep hounding it.

00:39:20.814 --> 00:39:22.440
And then people that are here
for five and a half years

00:39:22.440 --> 00:39:23.650
will go through something

00:39:23.650 --> 00:39:25.109
and then I'll get on the phone with them

00:39:25.109 --> 00:39:25.942
and they're like, yeah.

00:39:25.942 --> 00:39:27.357
And I'm like, why didn't
you come and talk to me?

00:39:27.357 --> 00:39:28.203
And they're like, yeah.

00:39:35.630 --> 00:39:37.740
So the local thing, I got it.

00:39:37.740 --> 00:39:41.915
- [Man] Yeah, well one of my
biggest issues is marketing.

00:39:41.915 --> 00:39:42.748
- Okay.

00:39:44.080 --> 00:39:45.100
- [Man] It's just not consistent.

00:39:45.100 --> 00:39:47.300
We outsource to another company

00:39:47.300 --> 00:39:49.550
and it just seems like
they're always kind of

00:39:51.230 --> 00:39:52.690
like I'm always in the dark with it.

00:39:52.690 --> 00:39:54.440
They're not very transparent.

00:39:54.440 --> 00:39:57.291
- Well you shouldn't, you
need to change that vendor.

00:39:57.291 --> 00:39:58.124
- [Man] Right.

00:39:58.124 --> 00:39:59.640
- Anybody you're paying, that
isn't willing to give you

00:39:59.640 --> 00:40:02.180
clean information, is a problem.

00:40:02.180 --> 00:40:03.520
Period, always.

00:40:03.520 --> 00:40:05.260
- [Man] And I've changed
them multiple times.

00:40:05.260 --> 00:40:07.713
- Yep, what about taking it internal?

00:40:08.575 --> 00:40:09.549
- [Man] That's what I
was going to ask you.

00:40:09.549 --> 00:40:10.490
Do you think that's smart of me to do--

00:40:10.490 --> 00:40:11.760
- You should taste it.

00:40:11.760 --> 00:40:12.723
You should try it.

00:40:13.760 --> 00:40:15.150
Yes, it's smart of you.

00:40:15.150 --> 00:40:17.820
You notice how I don't like
to do absolute answers.

00:40:17.820 --> 00:40:19.660
But based on multiple times,

00:40:19.660 --> 00:40:22.540
just learning what it looks
like, what it feels like

00:40:22.540 --> 00:40:24.080
is a good context point.

00:40:24.080 --> 00:40:25.290
Because when that doesn't work

00:40:25.290 --> 00:40:26.420
then you can step back and be like,

00:40:26.420 --> 00:40:28.310
okay this doesn't work, that doesn't work.

00:40:28.310 --> 00:40:29.970
Or when it works, you're like,
fuck, I should've done this

00:40:29.970 --> 00:40:31.520
all along.

00:40:31.520 --> 00:40:33.240
You just need a context point.

00:40:33.240 --> 00:40:34.890
There's so many things
I do that I actually

00:40:34.890 --> 00:40:36.070
don't think are gonna work,

00:40:36.070 --> 00:40:39.100
but I do them because I
need the reference point.

00:40:39.100 --> 00:40:41.040
That's actually how I
built all of VaynerMedia.

00:40:41.040 --> 00:40:42.717
Most of what I did at VaynerMedia,

00:40:42.717 --> 00:40:45.830
2019, 18, most of what
I did at VaynerMedia

00:40:45.830 --> 00:40:50.140
from 2015, '16, and '17, I
didn't even believe in fully.

00:40:50.140 --> 00:40:51.420
But I needed the context point

